 (whether a zero is a simple zero or a multiple zero) of the zeros.\n\nHowever, it is known that the Riemann zeta function has infinitely many non-trivial zeros, and it is conjectured that all of these zeros are simple. This conjecture about the simplicity of the zeros is independent of the Riemann Hypothesis.\n\nTo the best of our knowledge, the Riemann Hypothesis does not imply any information about the simplicity of the zeros. Therefore, the Riemann Hypothesis does not imply that any percentage of the Riemann zeros are known to be simple.\n\nThus, the answer is \\boxed{0\\%}."}]
