bb{P}^1$ of degree $2g-2$. This means that the preimage of a generic point in $\\mathbb{P}^1$ consists of $2g-2$ points, counted with multiplicity.\n\nThe maximum degree of a closed point on the curve $C$ can be achieved if a single point in $\\mathbb{P}^1$ has a preimage consisting of a single point on $C$ with multiplicity $2g-2$. This is possible because the degree of the morphism is $2g-2$, and it can be concentrated at a single point.\n\nTherefore, the maximum degree of a closed point on the curve $C$ is $2g-2$. The final answer is:\n\n\\boxed{2g-2}"}]
